# Findings gitleaks is right to flag on entropy, but which are intentionally public.
# Every entry needs a reason. If you cannot write one, it is not a false positive.

# share/config.js SHARE_TOKEN — deliberately public, not a credential.
#
# This is an 18-byte random value generated for this project. It is not a Cloudflare
# credential and Cloudflare has never seen it. It is compared against the share Worker's
# UPLOAD_TOKEN to gate PUT /u, and gates nothing else: reads need no token, there is no
# delete route, and no code path reaches any other resource.
#
# It ships inside a distributed browser extension, so it is readable by anyone who installs
# it. That is by design and is stated in the source. Treating it as a secret would be
# cargo-culting -- the real controls are the 12 MB size cap, the per-IP rate limit, the
# 7-day object TTL and the Workers Free daily request ceiling. See
# docs/adr/0001-remain-on-the-workers-free-plan.md.
#
# Blast radius if abused: 12 MB uploads to one R2 bucket, 20/min per IP, deleted after 7 days.
share/config.js:generic-api-key:16
